{
  "id": "inlay_hints/type_hints/02_type_sugar",
  "topic": "inlay_hints",
  "subtopic": "type_hints",
  "title": "Type sugar length limits",
  "summary": "Aliases keep their spelling, and an over-long type falls back to its sugared name",
  "prose": "A type without a spelling short enough is dropped, and default template arguments never print. The budget is `inlay_hints.type_name_limit`; `0` lifts it.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [
    "clangd#1298",
    "clangd#1357"
  ],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "using Integer = int;\n\nInteger make_alias();\n\ntemplate <typename A, typename B, typename C>\nstruct extremely_long_template_name {};\n\nusing Compact = extremely_long_template_name<int, char, bool>;\n\nCompact make_compact();\n\nextremely_long_template_name<Integer, Integer, Integer> make_long();\n\ntemplate <typename T, typename U = int>\nstruct Defaulted {};\n\nDefaulted<float> make_defaulted();\n\nvoid use() {\n    auto aliased = make_alias();\n    auto shortened = make_compact();\n    auto dropped = make_long();\n    auto defaulted = make_defaulted();\n}\n",
      "markers": []
    }
  ],
